g/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\"GitHub\", \"Microsoft\", \"AI\", \"GitHub-Copilot\", \"LLMs\", \"pricing\", \"coding-agents\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Firefox 150 includes 271 vulnerability fixes from Claude Mythos Preview\",\n    \"description\": \"Firefox CTO Bobby Holley shares their experience applying Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox, identifying and fixing 271 vulnerabilities. Holley notes that defenders finally have a chance to win decisively if teams shake off the vertigo and get to work.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Bobby Holley)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/firefox-150-claude/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"Claude\", \"AI\", \"Firefox\", \"Mozilla\", \"security\", \"AI-security-research\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Where's the raccoon with the ham radio? (ChatGPT Images 2.0)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0, with Sam Altman claiming the leap is equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5. Simon tests the new image generation model.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/chatgpt-images-2/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI\", \"image-generation\", \"OpenAI\", \"ChatGPT\", \"testing\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft and OpenAI end their exclusive and revenue-sharing deal\",\n    \"description\": \"Microsoft and OpenAI have ended their exclusive partnership deal, allowing OpenAI to pursue other computing partnerships while Microsoft can work with other AI companies. This marks a major shift in the AI landscape.\",\n    \"author\": \"Julie Bort\",\n    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/27/microsoft-openai-exclusive-deal-ends\",\n